- Make Calendar occupy the full available width of that dashboard section.
- Redesign the calendar as a clean, premium advisor schedule.
- Make meeting times, client names and purposes easy to scan.
- Use deliberate spacing and clear typography.
- Highlight the next relevant meeting without overwhelming the other events.
- Add a clear "Open Calendar" action leading to the full Calendar workspace.
- Reduce repeated paragraphs and unnecessary status labels.
- Keep existing meeting data and related client navigation intact.

The Calendar section should feel like the primary scheduling feature of the Dashboard, not another generic card.

Do not modify the rest of the Dashboard unless necessary for layout consistency.

## TASK 2: Move Follow-ups into the full Calendar workspace

Currently, the full Calendar has a small October 2026 monthly picker on the left.

Redesign that left area to become a dedicated Follow-ups sidebar.

Layout:
- Left: approximately 260–300px for Follow-ups.
- Center/right: flexible main calendar workspace.
- Calendar takes most of the screen width.

The sidebar should display:
- Follow-ups heading and outstanding count.
- Due Now, This Week, Later and Done filters.
- Compact, readable tasks.
- Task checkbox or completion control.
- Due dates and relevant client names.
- An Add Follow-up action.

