The original mini-month date picker should no longer permanently consume the sidebar. Move date navigation into the main calendar toolbar, with an optional compact date-picker popover.

## TASK 3: Add a fully functional Month view

The full Calendar currently has Day and Week controls.

Add Month as a third option.

Use a proper segmented control:

Day | Week | Month

Day view:
- Chronological meeting schedule.
- Readable event titles and times.
- Selected meeting details when needed.
- No overlapping event elements.

Week view:
- Seven-day calendar.
- Clearly labeled days and times.
- Meetings positioned in the correct day/time.
- Correct handling of concurrent and overlapping meetings.
- Events remain accessible even in crowded time slots.

Month view:
- Full seven-column monthly calendar.
- Correct weekday alignment.
- Five or six rows as required by the selected month.
- Correct previous/next month navigation.
- Meeting indicators or concise event labels.
- Overflow handling such as "+3 more" for crowded dates.
- Clicking a day opens its Day view.
- Clicking an event opens its details.
- Clear visual distinction between the selected date and actual today.

All three views must use the same calendar events and date-selection state.

Switching views must preserve the selected date and not unexpectedly reset the calendar.

The Follow-ups sidebar must remain present in all three views.

